<title>UK: London precious metals end mixed, gold weakening.</title>
<headline>London precious metals end mixed, gold weakening.</headline>
<text>
<p>GOLD - Closed at $339.50/$340.00 unchanged and just above opening level. No real upside and little interest after initial short covering. Turned lower post close.</p>
<p>SILVER - Finished two cents firmer at $4.74/$4.76.</p>
<p>PLATINUM - Ended $5.50 firmer at $413.00/$418.00. Early borrowing sparked short covering. Ended off day's high.</p>
<p>PALLADIUM - Finished at $196.00/$201.00 up $4.50.</p>
</text>
